  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HelpAge 2020-2024 - HelpAge 2020-2024 (New Strategy 2025-2029)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">HelpAge 2020-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Established in 1983, HelpAge International (HAI) is a civil society organisation that supports older people to claim their rights and challenge discrimination and poverty, so that they can lead dignified, secure, active and healthy lives.  The organization represents a global network of civil society organisations working to promote and protect the rights of older women and men in nearly 90 countries, with over 157 member organisations, the majority of which are located in Low and Middle Income Countries (LMICs). HAI works with a wide range of activities, covering advocacy, development and humanitarian operations.

In the previous collaboration (2015-2019), core funding from Sida supported a 5 year strategy (2015-2020) with a focus on income, health and care, voice and inclusion (gender and disability). During this period, HAI has specifically strengthened their work with health systems strengthening (also in collaboration with WHO), Non Communicable Diseases (NCDs), including mental health, and mainstreaming gender equality and inclusion (focus on disability). 

This contribution refers to  core funding support from Sida to enable HAI to implement their new 10 year strategy (2020-2030). The 2030 strategy identifies 10 focus areas (including health and education) to achieve a positive impact on the quality of life of the poorest older people, with a focus on wellbeing, dignity and voice. Of the 10 focus areas, the 2020-22 planning priorities include: 1. Inspire a movement for change; 2. Promote age-inclusive systems; 3. Champion healthy ageing; 4. Deliver inclusive humanitarian action; 5. Challenge violence, abuse and neglect. Complementary to the Core Activities, additional support targets HAI&apos;s Global COVID-19 Response Plan. An amendment of agreement for nexus-support to the Ukraine crises was decided in March 2022.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">HelpAge International (HAI), som grundades 1983, &#xe4;r en civilsamh&#xe4;llsorganisation som st&#xf6;djer &#xe4;ldre att h&#xe4;vda sina r&#xe4;ttigheter och minska diskriminering och fattigdom bland &#xe4;ldre s&#xe5; att de kan leva v&#xe4;rdiga, s&#xe4;kra, aktiva och h&#xe4;lsosamma liv. Organisationen representerar ett globalt n&#xe4;tverk av civilsamh&#xe4;llsorganisationer som arbetar f&#xf6;r att fr&#xe4;mja och skydda &#xe4;ldre kvinnors och m&#xe4;ns r&#xe4;ttigheter i n&#xe4;stan 90 l&#xe4;nder, med &#xf6;ver 157 medlemsorganisationer, varav huvuddelen ligger i l&#xe5;g- och medelinkomstl&#xe4;nder (LMIC). HAI arbetar med ett brett spektrum av aktiviteter f&#xf6;r p&#xe5;verkansarbete och l&#xe5;ngsiktig h&#xe5;llbar utveckling samt humanit&#xe4;ra insatser.

Under det tidigare samarbetet (2015-2019) st&#xf6;dde Sidas k&#xe4;rnfinansiering en 5-&#xe5;rig strategi (2015-2020) med fokus p&#xe5; inkomst, h&#xe4;lsa och v&#xe5;rd, r&#xf6;st och inkludering (k&#xf6;n och funktionshinder). Under den perioden st&#xe4;rkte HAI s&#xe4;rskilt sitt arbete med h&#xe4;lsosystem (delvis i samarbete med WHO), icke-&#xf6;verf&#xf6;rbara sjukdomar (NCD) inkluderande mental h&#xe4;lsa, och sitt arbete med att integrera j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och inkludering av k&#xf6;n (fokus p&#xe5; funktionshinder).

Detta bidrag avser k&#xe4;rnfinansieringsst&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n Sida f&#xf6;r att HAI ska kunna p&#xe5;b&#xf6;rja implementeringen av sin nya 10-&#xe5;riga strategi (2020-2030). 2030-strategin identifierar 10 fokusomr&#xe5;den (inklusive h&#xe4;lsa och utbildning) f&#xf6;r att uppn&#xe5; en positiv inverkan p&#xe5; livskvaliteten f&#xf6;r de fattigaste &#xe4;ldre med fokus p&#xe5; v&#xe4;lbefinnande, v&#xe4;rdighet och r&#xf6;st. Av de tio fokusomr&#xe5;dena inkluderar prioriteringarna f&#xf6;r planeringen 2020-22; 1. Inspirera en r&#xf6;relse f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndring; 2. Fr&#xe4;mja &#xe5;ldersinkluderande system. 3. Fr&#xe4;mja h&#xe4;lsosamt &#xe5;ldrande; 4. Leverera inkluderande humanit&#xe4;ra insatser; 5. Motverka v&#xe5;ld, &#xf6;vergrepp och f&#xf6;rsummelse. Som ett komplement till k&#xe4;rnverksamheten innefattar detta beslut &#xe4;ven st&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n Sida att  t&#xe4;cka HAI: s Globala COVID-19 Handlings Plan. Ett till&#xe4;ggsbeslut om nexusst&#xf6;d samband med Ukrainakrisen tog i mars 2022.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">HelpAge has had support for its strategic plan during 2020-2024. 

In May 2025 an agreement amendment was decided to a health focused programme that will contribute to achieving impact for older people in Ethiopia, Tanzania, Pakistan, and Ukraine so they can experience improved health and wellbeing through more inclusive, integrated, and age-responsive health systems that advance Universal Health Coverage (UHC).

The programme will contribute to the impact by achieving the programme goal :
- To improve the integration of community-based, person-centred care for older people particularly through ICOPE and NCD interventions into national health systems, services and  policy frameworks in Ethiopia, Tanzania, Pakistan, and Ukraine while building knowledge and  advocacy for broader uptake.

HelpAge will achieve the programme goal through the delivery of three outcomes. 

Outcome 1: Community level initiatives - Demonstrated models of best practice in community-based health and care services through the piloting of ICOPE and integrated NCD  interventions in Ethiopia, Tanzania, and Pakistan using context specific interventions that  contribute to the advancement of Universal Health Coverage that is responsive to the needs of  an ageing population.

Outcome 2:  National level advocacy - Context appropriate progress made via National-level  advocacy for the inclusion of ICOPE and non-communicable disease (NCD) prevention,  management, and treatment within Ministry of Health training programs and basic health  service packages in Tanzania, Ethiopia, Pakistan and Ukraine, fostering a sustainable and  inclusive healthcare system for older adults.

Outcome 3: Global level - Strengthened body of knowledge and best practices on community based Integrated Care for Older People (ICOPE) and NCD prevention, through collaboration and engagement with key stakeholders, including members of the HelpAge Healthy Ageing Platform, the World Health Organization (WHO), and other global health bodies.</narrative>
  </description>
